<description>
Extend the inner-color leaf markers into full row and column cuts through the foreground rectangle.

Input structure
- A black background contains one solid rectangular foreground region.
- The rectangle uses exactly two colors: an outer color at all four corners and an inner color mass.
- Single-cell leaf protrusions of the inner color stick into the outer-color margin.

Rule
- A leaf whose only inner-color neighbor is above or below selects its column; a leaf whose neighbor is left or right selects its row.
- Selected rows and columns are recolored to the outer color inside the foreground rectangle.
- The same selected rows and columns are extended through the background outside the rectangle using the inner color.

Key insight
- The protruding leaf pixels are not noise: each is a control marker naming one row or column to cut through the rectangle and continue outward.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_along_path",
  "src": "single-cell inner-color leaf markers attached to the inner color mass inside the foreground rectangle",
  "path": "a leaf attached vertically selects its column; a leaf attached horizontally selects its row; extend that axis from the rectangle to the canvas edge",
  "trajectory": "paint background cells outside the rectangle on the selected row or column with the inner color",
  "transform": "inside the rectangle, recolor the full selected row or column to the outer corner color"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 13-19 rows x 13-18 cols
  background: black (0)
  colors: 2 distinct non-black colors — outer_color and inner_color
  rectangle:
    structure: solid foreground rectangle on black background, no other objects
    frame: outer_color border exactly 2 cells thick on all 4 sides
    fill: rect[2:-2, 2:-2] is solid inner_color
    size: 8-13 rows x 11-14 cols
    margins: >=1 cell of background on every side
  markers:
    count: 2-3 inner_color cells embedded in the 2nd ring of the frame
    placement: each marker at depth 1 from the rectangle edge (penultimate frame layer)
    neighbor: exactly 1 inner_color 4-neighbor (the adjacent inner fill cell toward interior)
    axis: vertical neighbor -> selects column; horizontal neighbor -> selects row
    selected_axis: must pass through inner fill region (local index 2..rect_dim-3)
    separation: markers on the same side must be non-adjacent (gap >= 2 cells)
    mix: 1 row marker + 1-2 col markers [observed]; total 2-3
  output:
    selected_columns: outer_color through entire rect column, inner_color from rect edge to grid edge (top and bottom)
    selected_rows: outer_color through entire rect row, inner_color from rect edge to grid edge (left and right)
    rows applied after columns at intersections inside rect (both yield outer_color)

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first, then remove trajectory lines to get input
  steps:
    1. Pick grid dims (13-19 x 13-18), two non-black colors (outer, inner)
    2. Place rectangle (8-13 x 11-14) with >=1 margin on all sides
    3. Fill rectangle — outer_color frame width 2, inner_color fill inside
    4. Choose 2-3 marker axes — 1 row + 1-2 cols [observed], each indexing an inner fill row/col
    5. Build output — draw full outer_color cuts through rect and inner_color extensions to grid edges
    6. Derive input — start from the output, undo the cuts (restore inner_color inside rect, restore black outside rect on selected axes), then place each marker cell in the 2nd ring on the appropriate side
    7. For each marker, pick which side it protrudes from (any of the 4 frame sides aligned with its axis); ensure non-adjacency if sharing a side
```
